{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>To lift, lips of, mouth of</b> — three joined [forms]. And likewise the interpretation: it is not good to lift the face of a wicked one in his judgment, and likewise a righteous one in his judgment, for he is acquitted. And 'lips of a fool' is the aforementioned wicked one, whose lips bring about that he comes into strife, and his mouth brings him into strife on account of blows — that is, on account of that which happens to him to strike his fellow and strike him. And behold, his mouth gives a blow to himself, and his lips bring about a snare for his soul. And it is not good to lift his face."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:28.551814568Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}